SUMMARY:Thanksgiving Potluck Luncheon
DESCRIPTION:The Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Asheville (UUAVL) and the Unitarian Universalist Congregation of the Swannanoa Valley (UUSV) are teaming up for this year’s Thanksgiving Potluck Luncheon. Please sign up in Sandburg Hall after services to bring a covered dish and to volunteer for setup\, takedown\, or one of the two kitchen crews. Attendees will arrive at 11:30 AM on Thanksgiving Day\, participate in a short service\, enjoy a delicious meal\, and go for a walk in the neighborhood afterward. We would like to encourage diners to bring a plant-based dish. Also\, please supply your own plate and utensils and bring a bag for taking them home. (To save time and labor\, the kitchen crew will wash only cups after the meal.)
URL:https://uuasheville.org/event/thanksgiving-potluck-lunch-2026/
LOCATION:1 Sandburg Hall/Kitchen\, 1 Edwin Pl\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:*Newcomer-Friendly - LOVING,*Social Groups - LOVING,Featured Upcoming,Other,`Holiday
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://uuasheville.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thanksgiving-Potluck-eNews-Graphic-Square.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Ellen Welles":MAILTO:ewelles@bellsouth.net
END:VEVENT
